cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite package "knowledge" in publications use:'
type: software
license: MIT
title: 'knowledge: Fisheries Evidence and Tuned Habitat Thresholds for BC Watershed
  Groups'
version: 0.4.13
abstract: 'Gathers fisheries evidence for British Columbia watershed groups (provincial
  fish sampling records, past reports, cited literature values with their quotes,
  intrinsic-potential models and life-history timing) and tunes from the fish records
  the gradient and stream-size thresholds that the link habitat models use: it places
  sampling visits on link''s stream segments, scores candidate rules on held-out watershed
  groups, grades segments by expected use, and tabulates, maps and compares the tuned
  rules with link''s defaults. It also pulls PSCIS crossing layers and past-report
  tables for a group and checks stream names before a search. Under active development.'
